      ":question/problem": "Express $\\frac{5}{3}-\\frac{10}{3}\\sin^2\\left(127^\\circ\\right)$ as a single trigonometric ratio.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Collect the common factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\frac{5}{3}-\\frac{10}{3}\\sin^2\\left(127^\\circ\\right)\\\\&=\\frac{5}{3}\\left(1-2\\sin^2\\left(127^\\circ\\right)\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the alternative cosine double-angle formula:\n\n$$\n1-2\\sin^2 x=\\cos(2x)\n$$\n\nSubstitute $x=127^\\circ$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n1-2\\sin^2\\left(127^\\circ\\right)&=\\cos\\left(2\\cdot 127^\\circ\\right)\\\\&=\\cos\\left(254^\\circ\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeep the outside factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{5}{3}\\left(1-2\\sin^2\\left(127^\\circ\\right)\\right)&=\\frac{5}{3}\\cos\\left(254^\\circ\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
